+/* ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
+ * ZPASS occlusion reports (NV4097 SET_ZPASS_PIXEL_COUNT_ENABLE 0x1D84,
+ * CLEAR_REPORT_VALUE 0x17C8, GET_REPORT 0x1800 type 1).
+ *
+ * The FIFO walker used to answer every ZPASS report with 0xFFFF ("visible"),
+ * so Demon's Souls drew its sun glare and lens flares at full strength even
+ * with the sun behind a wall. Counting runs as D3D12 occlusion queries: one
+ * query per enabled segment (a segment also ends at a command-list flush,
+ * since a query cannot span lists, and at each GET_REPORT); a report is the
+ * sum of the segments since the last CLEAR. The result arrives once the GPU
+ * has passed the report's fence; until then the walker writes the last value
+ * delivered for that report slot (rsx_live_draw_zpass_report). LD_ZPASS=0
+ * keeps the old always-visible answer.
